## qubes-vpn: what the vpn-manager qube may do, and nothing more.
##
## Install in dom0 as /etc/qubes/policy.d/30-qubes-vpn.policy (see
## docs/install.md). Qubes 4.2 format:
##   service  argument  source  target  action  [options]
## Anything no rule allows is denied. Lower-numbered files are read first.
##
## Qubes taken part:
##   @tag:vpn          VPN qubes (provides_network=True, agent installed)
##   @tag:vpn-client   qubes the manager may move between net qubes

## The agents in the VPN qubes (agent/qubes-rpc). They run as root there:
## the tunnels, nft and /rw/config/vpn need it. autostart=no: asking a
## halted VPN qube must not start it; the manager starts qubes only through
## admin.vm.Start, when asked to.
vpn.Status        *  vpn-manager  @tag:vpn  allow user=root autostart=no
vpn.Stats         *  vpn-manager  @tag:vpn  allow user=root autostart=no
vpn.ListProfiles  *  vpn-manager  @tag:vpn  allow user=root autostart=no
vpn.Connect       *  vpn-manager  @tag:vpn  allow user=root autostart=no
vpn.Disconnect    *  vpn-manager  @tag:vpn  allow user=root autostart=no

## Settings, one line per key: the key is the argument, the value comes on
## stdin and the agent checks it. Leave out a line to keep that setting out
## of the manager's reach; credentials in particular means the OpenVPN
## password passes through vpn-manager (it is stored only in the VPN qube).
vpn.Configure  +autoconnect  vpn-manager  @tag:vpn  allow user=root autostart=no
vpn.Configure  +ping_target  vpn-manager  @tag:vpn  allow user=root autostart=no
vpn.Configure  +credentials  vpn-manager  @tag:vpn  allow user=root autostart=no

## The qube list. qubesd answers admin.vm.List with only the qubes this
## policy lets vpn-manager list, so the first line is the call and the next
## two say which qubes it returns.
admin.vm.List          *            vpn-manager  @adminvm         allow target=dom0
admin.vm.List          *            vpn-manager  @tag:vpn         allow target=dom0
admin.vm.List          *            vpn-manager  @tag:vpn-client  allow target=dom0

## Which list a qube is on, whether it runs, its net qube and address (the
## address maps vif counters to qubes). Net qube and address of VPN qubes
## too: chains (VPN over VPN), and a VPN qube behind another one.
admin.vm.tag.Get       +vpn         vpn-manager  @tag:vpn         allow target=dom0
admin.vm.tag.Get       +vpn         vpn-manager  @tag:vpn-client  allow target=dom0
admin.vm.tag.Get       +vpn-client  vpn-manager  @tag:vpn         allow target=dom0
admin.vm.tag.Get       +vpn-client  vpn-manager  @tag:vpn-client  allow target=dom0
admin.vm.CurrentState  *            vpn-manager  @tag:vpn         allow target=dom0
admin.vm.CurrentState  *            vpn-manager  @tag:vpn-client  allow target=dom0
admin.vm.property.Get  +netvm       vpn-manager  @tag:vpn         allow target=dom0
admin.vm.property.Get  +netvm       vpn-manager  @tag:vpn-client  allow target=dom0
admin.vm.property.Get  +ip          vpn-manager  @tag:vpn         allow target=dom0
admin.vm.property.Get  +ip          vpn-manager  @tag:vpn-client  allow target=dom0

## Starting and stopping VPN qubes.
admin.vm.Start         *            vpn-manager  @tag:vpn         allow target=dom0
admin.vm.Shutdown      *            vpn-manager  @tag:vpn         allow target=dom0

## Moving a client qube to another net qube: through dom0's vpn.SetNetvm,
## whose policy names each net qube allowed (31-qubes-vpn-setnetvm.policy).
##
## The line below is the alternative without any code in dom0, for
## netvm_method = admin in the manager's config.ini. It is off on purpose: a
## policy cannot limit the VALUE written, so a vpn-manager taken over through
## a VPN qube's answers could give every vpn-client qube ANY net qube
## (sys-net, say) and route it around the VPNs.
#admin.vm.property.Set  +netvm       vpn-manager  @tag:vpn-client  allow target=dom0
